<title>USA: Bard selling product line to Conmed.</title>
<headline>Bard selling product line to Conmed.</headline>
<dateline>MURRAY HILL, N.J. 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>C.R. Bard Inc said Thursday it has reached a definitive agreement to sell its surgical suction product line to Conmed Corp.</p>
<p>Terms of the sale were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The product line, with annual revenue of about $25 million, is currently distributed through Bard's medical division under the Davol and Bard trademarks.</p>
<p>The company expects the deal to close within 60 days.</p>
<p>C.R. Bard makes and sells health care products.</p>
</text>
